{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/786015-do-vampires-necessarily-have-high-banality","id":786015,"title":"Do Vampires necessarily have high banality?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-14T09:09:59-08:00","id":786015,"title":"Do Vampires necessarily have high banality?","content":"Hey guys,so i'm new to Dreaming. i started reading the book recently. i've noticed that in few first books there a lot of references to the fact that vampires are really caked with banality. but that doesnt seem to make much sense to me,like: banality is about boredom,about being insignifcant,banality is created by the lack of wonder,lack of imagination,banality is created by inipid tv shows,by working borings jobs everyday,by never travelling,never doing anything fun,unexpected or cool or badass.<br /> But vampires?<br /> Vampires lives for severallifetimes,Vampires have suprpowers,some control minds,other can become fith times sexier,others read minds,other fly,some becoming prince sof the underworld controlling a mass army of dark underlings,vampires eat people. All in all,a vampire life is not boring,it's dangerous bloody scary but not boring,they dont lack imagination,they have to be imaginative so they can figure it out a way of nobody stabbing them in the back,vampires do things that seems take out of fantasy books all the time. to survive in their cutthroat byzantine society,they do unexpected,coll and badass things.<br /> All in all,i always thoght vampires are chock full of wonder,their wonder are dark,bloody,scary or even evil,but it's wonder. they're nto banal or boring<br /> so,am i right? or my logic missing some important detail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T09:18:43-08:00","id":786021,"title":"","content":"The RAW say they do, because they're all death-y and stuff. No, it doesn't make a lot of sense if you think too hard about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T09:28:15-08:00","id":786032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/786015-do-vampires-necessarily-have-high-banality?p=786021#post786021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The RAW say they do, because they're all death-y and stuff. No, it doesn't make a lot of sense if you think too hard about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>my current rule of thumb is that if a being,in ay way shape or form,it's not boring,it cant be banal enough to risk a changeling glamour","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T10:43:00-08:00","id":786078,"title":"","content":"The more logical argument in the books is that vampires are Banal because they're unchanging, and have lost the spark of true creativity that empowers Glamour when their souls were messed up by becoming vampires.<br /> <br /> The issue is more that CtD's current books <i>suck</i> at defining Banality in a consistent way. Banality is not just about whether or not something is boring (that would make for very bad antagonists if what makes them dangerous is that they're boring).<br /> <br /> That said, vampires, like all categories of things, don't have a single Banality rating. Certain Clans and Bloodlines are going to have relatively low Banality (Malkavians, Toreador, Kiasyd, etc.), and individuals can differ from the general ratings presented in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T11:48:35-08:00","id":786107,"title":"","content":"PCs do increadibly interesting and exiciting things because they are Pcs. the &quot;Average&quot; vampire is kind of boring. They feed. They keep their head low they stick to a routine that doesn't change much over the centuries until they have PC moments. But a 500 year old elder probably has only had maybe 20 years of &quot;Adventure&quot; most of its &quot;Wake up, feed, keep status quo&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T10:27:05-08:00","id":786787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/786015-do-vampires-necessarily-have-high-banality?p=786107#post786107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PCs do increadibly interesting and exiciting things because they are Pcs. the &quot;Average&quot; vampire is kind of boring. They feed. They keep their head low they stick to a routine that doesn't change much over the centuries until they have PC moments. But a 500 year old elder probably has only had maybe 20 years of &quot;Adventure&quot; most of its &quot;Wake up, feed, keep status quo&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And 500 years of doing the same thing (eat, sleep, drain, repeat) IS boring. Repetition, lack of creativity and stasis are the hallmarks of Banality, however, rather than mere boredom (which is more a by-product of those things).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T23:38:13-08:00","id":787879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/786015-do-vampires-necessarily-have-high-banality?p=786787#post786787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And 500 years of doing the same thing (eat, sleep, drain, repeat) IS boring. Repetition, lack of creativity and stasis are the hallmarks of Banality, however, rather than mere boredom (which is more a by-product of those things).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I am saying Being a supernatural being isn't an Intrinsically Glamourous state which is where the Op is coming from. Most vampires spend most of their time doing boring things. Just like most people aren't Dreamers.<br /> <br /> So I don't agree either with the &quot;vampires should be banal for being vampires&quot; or &quot;Vampires should be less banal&quot; they should have the same judgement calls as humans just based perhaps on different life situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T02:34:55-08:00","id":787939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/786015-do-vampires-necessarily-have-high-banality?p=787879#post787879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I am saying Being a supernatural being isn't an Intrinsically Glamourous state which is where the Op is coming from. Most vampires spend most of their time doing boring things. Just like most people aren't Dreamers.<br /> <br /> So I don't agree either with the &amp;quot;vampires should be banal for being vampires&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Vampires should be less banal&amp;quot; they should have the same judgement calls as humans just based perhaps on different life situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fluff is inconsistent, but it is stated multiple times that vampires lack the creative spark. They can't experience true inspiration and create something new because of their inherent curse (a metaphorical extension of 'eat only ashes', etc). That probably puts a dampener on their Glamour.<br /> <br /> Do vampires even dream? I expect theirs are the dreams of prophecy and damnation, rather than the dreams of hope and wonder humans have - if they dream at all.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, humans (who are typically Banality 7+ anyway), can create and reproduce and dream. It makes sense, therefore, that most vampires are at least as Banal as humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T04:57:02-08:00","id":787994,"title":"","content":"There's also the Masquerade to consider. An army of vampires working to keep humanity from noticing the supernatural, from putting two and two together . . . The Kindred don't <i>want</i> humans thinking about vampires, or faeries, or anything like that. They want the humans to stay focused on their mundane lives, not rocking the boat, just keeping their collective head down and breeding more blood &quot;donors&quot; . . . From a changeling perspective, the Camarilla is basically an alliance of undead Autumn People.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/786015-do-vampires-necessarily-have-high-banality?p=786078#post786078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .That said, vampires, like all categories of things, don't have a single Banality rating. Certain Clans and Bloodlines are going to have relatively low Banality (Malkavians, Toreador, Kiasyd, etc.), and individuals can differ from the general ratings presented in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's also Elizabeth, a Boston-based Malkavian who is <i>absolutely</i> convinced that she <i>is</i> a changeling<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T06:21:22-08:00","id":788032,"title":"","content":"In the 2nd ed corebook appendix, at least, the fluff talks about how vampire banality may or may not exist, but the chart puts them at 8-10...except Malkavians, who are at 6. Toreadors, Kiasyd, Ravnos, and the like don't get a specific callout; maybe they're at 7? I'd agree that vampirism in and of itself shouldn't put banality above 7, but the more repetitive/corporate/Weaver-influenced/unchanging one is, the higher their banality. So anarchs and neonates, sure, they could be at 7, maybe 6, but it's an okay rule of thumb to say vamps are banal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T09:03:56-08:00","id":788143,"title":"","content":"Well... as far as I remember (and my changeling-do is rather rusty), Banality and Glamour are linked to how people &quot;feel&quot;, sensations and creative skills. An furthermore, apparently, the Glamour Changeling can perceive is based on personal perceptions (like the Ailil that take Glamour from politics, or something similar...)<br /> The problem, with vampires, is that they're mostly cynical beings, and cynical is a really Banal thing. Therefore, the Glamour Changeling can perceive is rather rare.<br /> But maybe this isn't always the case.<br /> For example, as Ailil can take Glamour from political machinations, their best friends would be Ventrue or Elders in general. Red Cap and the Sabbat rank and file can probably be BFF. And if a Gangrel isn't hungry I can see why a Pooka or maybe even a Satyr can be attracted by his wild side.<br /> Ok... Satyrs can be attracted even by Toreador, Janette or most of the things that walk around, but that's another issue.<br /> <br /> That said,<br /> -Toreador can have the &quot;creative spark&quot; (1st Clanbook Toreador even implemented a system for those Toreador that had a &quot;creative spark&quot; for using it and making artworks)<br /> -Malkavian are a raw concentrate of emotions<br /> -Kyasid are halfbreed vampire-fae<br /> -Ravnos interweave chimeric reality with reality on daily basis (with their proprietary Discipline of Chimerism)<br /> -your friendly next-door-Nosferatu can be very openminded<br /> -the Gangrel self-of-wonder often push them on the road, &quot;banal&quot; people can call them vagrants but maybe a Changeling could see them as the last explorers in this world","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 12-17-2015, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T04:32:32-08:00","id":788662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/786015-do-vampires-necessarily-have-high-banality?p=787939#post787939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fluff is inconsistent, but it is stated multiple times that vampires lack the creative spark. They can't experience true inspiration and create something new because of their inherent curse (a metaphorical extension of 'eat only ashes', etc). That probably puts a dampener on their Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is inconsistent, I put &quot;vampires are intrinsically banal&quot; up there with &quot;Science is intrinsically banal&quot; Broad ranging and missing the point. There are Vampires who lose their spark, but the same is true of mortal dreamers. There are also vampires who become artists upon transition, this is just from the toreador perspective. We can talk about Ravnos and Malkavians next but lets look at things more broadly there has to be a level of creativity in the political games they play simply because they are different enough from human nature. That's before we get into new powers and belief systems <br /> <br /> So I find the idea that vampire lack the &quot;spark&quot; highly inconsistant with the rest of the fluff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do vampires even dream? I expect theirs are the dreams of prophecy and damnation, rather than the dreams of hope and wonder humans have - if they dream at all. </div> </div> </div>I've seen fluff which shows they dream, with some set of powers that push towards it being used as prophecy but nothing that says all of it such.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile, humans (who are typically Banality 7+ anyway), can create and reproduce and dream. It makes sense, therefore, that most vampires are at least as Banal as humans. </div> </div> </div><br /> I never said they should be any less than humans. I think Vampires should have the same range of Banalities as humans rather than having one set for each. For example I don't think Malkavians should get a different number than a Human with the same derangement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}